A quick Google search of the error revealed this post at stackoverflow.

http://stackoverflow.com/questions/16638297/vegdist-error-message-in-vegan-package

Apparently rows or columns containing only zeros will cause this error.  Indeed, your subset does contain rows that are only filled with zeros.  I don't use these algorithms so unfortunately I can't advise an alternative workaround.

sitebeeall<-table(all.bee$sitetype, all.bee$g_sp)
rowSums(sitebeeall)
rowSums(sitebee12)

Brian

